# Nexora — Cursor rules

Read `CLAUDE.md` before making changes.

## Conventions (summary)

See `CLAUDE.md` for full detail. In short:

- Server secrets stay server-side; browser uses anon key + RLS only.
- `VITE_` prefix means public bundle — never for secrets.
- RLS on all tables. Zod at boundaries. External content is untrusted.
- No hardcoded model IDs, thresholds, or secrets.
- Real-behaviour tests. Focused diffs. Never commit unless asked.

## Build plan

Run phases from `BUILD_SEQUENCE.md` one at a time, in order.

After each phase:

```bash
npm run typecheck && npm run build && npm test
```
